  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Fire Atlas",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"The Fire Atlas\"**\n\nAmerican fire insurance atlases mapped every block to answer one question: is this building a good risk? StrataIQ prints that same sheet for one address. The ground is deep atlas blue, content sits on cool white map sheets, and everything is a flat fill with a thin ink outline, as if printed rather than rendered.\n\nColor is a legend here, not decoration. A founder with no data background can read where any number came from by its color, and a printed key says so on the map. The real city is the hero: real buildings and streets in atlas colors, with the words printed straight onto it as label strips.\n\nPublic pages move a lot and tie that motion to the scroll, on one uninterrupted camera shot. Signed-in screens are denser and calmer, with the same materials on a cooler page. The system rejects the SaaS hero with a floating dashboard, and dark dashboards with glowing charts.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Atlas blue ground, cool white map sheets, flat fills, 1px ink outlines, square corners.",
      "A fixed color key for evidence: pink measured, yellow yours, stone estimated.",
      "Verdict colors kept apart from the key: green, red and ink.",
      "Exactly one yellow next step on a screen.",
      "Headlines printed as strips on the live map.",
      "One continuous camera shot under the landing story."
    ],
    "rules": [
